<Project>

  <!--
    NuGet audit suppressions — SixLabors.ImageSharp 1.0.4 (transitive).

    WHERE IT COMES FROM: PdfSharpCore 1.3.67 (TurboDocs PDF generation) hard-depends on
    SixLabors.ImageSharp 1.0.4 for raster image embedding. The .NET 10 SDK audits transitive
    packages by default, so these 7 advisories surface on every build of a PdfSharpCore consumer
    (Core + the three Revit shims).

    WHY SUPPRESSED RATHER THAN UPGRADED:
      - ImageSharp fixed these in 2.x/3.x, but those dropped net48 — and we ship a net48 (Revit 2024)
        channel for a couple more years, so a direct bump is not an option. PdfSharpCore also pins
        1.0.4 as a floor and would break against a force-overridden 2.x/3.x.
      - Real exposure is negligible: every XImage.FromFile in the codebase decodes a FIRM-CONFIGURED
        branding asset (Settings LogoFilePath / CoverBranding*Path), never untrusted or per-run image
        input. Cut-sheet merging uses XPdfForm (PDF parsing), not ImageSharp. The advisories require
        feeding a maliciously-crafted image to the decoder — not a path reachable here.

    Scoped to these specific advisory IDs (NOT a blanket NoWarn) so a genuinely NEW ImageSharp
    advisory would still surface. Root-cause fix is migrating PdfSharpCore -> PDFsharp 6.x (no
    ImageSharp dependency, net48-compatible); tracked separately.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2cmq-823j-5qj8" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5x7m-6737-26cr" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-63p8-c4ww-9cg7" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-65x7-c272-7g7r" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-g85r-6x2q-45w7" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qxrv-gp6x-rc23" />
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rxmq-m78w-7wmc" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
